[[Skyrim:Morokei (item)|Morokei]] is a moonstone [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest|dragon priest]] [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest Mask|mask]] gained by killing [[Skyrim:Morokei (creature)|Morokei]] within [[Skyrim:Labyrinthian|Labyrinthian]]. The mask's enchantment doubles [[Skyrim:Regenerate Magicka|magicka regeneration]]. It can be [[Skyrim:Workbench|improved]] with [[Skyrim:Refined Moonstone|refined moonstone]].<includeonly>

For more information, see the [[Skyrim:Morokei (item)|Morokei]] article.</includeonly><noinclude>
{{NewLeft}}

==Notes==
* Placing Morokei on its pedestal at [[Skyrim:Bromjunaar Sanctuary|Bromjunaar Sanctuary]] will remove any bonuses that it gained from tempering.
* Morokei has the second lowest armor rating of the masks, only slightly higher than that of the [[Skyrim:Wooden Mask|Wooden Mask]].
* All dragon priest masks are considered to be circlets in terms of equipment slots, meaning that they can be worn simultaneously with some bugged items, as detailed under [[Skyrim:Circlet|circlets]].
* Morokei means "Glorious" in the [[Lore:Dragon Language|dragon language]].
* [[Skyrim:Hendraheim (place)|Hendraheim]]{{CC|Hendraheim}}, [[Skyrim:Shadowfoot Sanctum (place)|Shadowfoot Sanctum]]{{CC|Shadowfoot Sanctum}}, [[Skyrim:Tundra Homestead (place)|Tundra Homestead]]'s cellar{{CC|Tundra Homestead}}, [[Skyrim:Bloodchill Manor|Bloodchill Cavern]]{{CC|Bloodchill Manor}}, and [[Skyrim:Myrwatch (place)|Myrwatch]]'s gallery{{CC|Myrwatch}} contain a [[Skyrim:Special Holder|special holder]] for this item.

